\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{The rotation-only matter operator}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{On the \vocabk{rotational cochains}{fdip-00YN}, define
inverse-link transport coefficientwise by
##{(T_i^R f)_I(x)=A(R_i(x))^{-1}f_I(x+\varepsilon_i).}
On the cubical factor, #{u_i\wedge} is left exterior multiplication
and #{u_i\cdot} is contraction with the dual basis vector: it
deletes #{u_i} with its position sign and is zero when #{u_i}
is absent. Both act as the identity on the internal factor.
The \newvocab{rotation-only matter operators} are
##{\begin{aligned}
\extd_R&=\sum_i(u_i\wedge)(T_i^R-\bbI),\\
\extdag_R&=\sum_i(u_i\cdot)((T_i^R)^{-1}-\bbI),\\
\extD_R&=\extd_R+\extdag_R,\\
\cov_R&=\extd_R-\extdag_R.
\end{aligned}}
Here
#{((T_i^R)^{-1}f)_I(x)=A(R_i(x-\varepsilon_i))f_I(x-\varepsilon_i)}.
The subscript records the entire collection of rotational links.}
